Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:19:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 13/52] kernel: clear the pulsed bits of a simple event

sceKernelPulseEvent clears every bit it pulsed, including ones that were already set.

(cherry picked from commit 0a4b5f026832ca678804f0098ac5afd5a31a5919)
---
 vita3k/kernel/src/sync_primitives.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vita3k/kernel/src/sync_primitives.cpp b/vita3k/kernel/src/sync_primitives.cpp
index 9e579f21..170b7f09 100644
--- a/vita3k/kernel/src/sync_primitives.cpp
+++ b/vita3k/kernel/src/sync_primitives.cpp
@@ -121,8 +121,9 @@ SceInt32 SimpleEvent::set_or_pulse(SceUInt32 set_pattern, SceUInt64 user_data, b
         return true;
     });
 
+    // A pulse clears its own bits, the others go back to what they were
     if (!is_set) {
-        pattern = old_pattern;
+        pattern = old_pattern & ~set_pattern;
         last_user_data = old_user_data;
     }
 
